  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Nevada received $261M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. Nevada recorded 396 awards with an average award size of $658K. Nevada obligations fell 92.9% year over year. Nevada obligations for FY27 are a partial fiscal-year total; prior full fiscal years were $3.3B in FY22, $3.8B in FY23, $4.1B in FY24, $4.1B in FY25, and $3.7B in FY26. The Department of Energy is the largest buyer in Nevada in FY2027 to date with $225M in obligations. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC is the largest vendor in Nevada in FY2027 to date with $225M in obligations. Facilities Support Services is the top industry in Nevada in FY2027 to date with $225M in obligations. Other agencies and vendors appear at much smaller scales in FY2027 to date, with the Department of Veterans Affairs at $20.8M and the second-largest vendor at $5.3M. These figures reflect obligations only and represent fiscal year to date totals for FY2027.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Nevada obligations fell 92.9% year over year. Nevada obligations in FY27 are $261M compared with full fiscal-year totals of $3.7B in FY26 and earlier multi-year levels above $3.3B. Nevada award count is 396 and average award size is $658K for FY2027 to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate Nevada spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Energy obligated $225M in Nevada in FY2027 to date. MISSION SUPPORT & TEST SERVICES LLC received $225M in obligations and Facilities Support Services totaled $225M in obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs and the next largest vendors and industries are much smaller, with the VA at $20.8M and the second-largest vendor at $5.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
